om the reviewed accessible data and remains unverified as phrased."", ""UNVERIFIED: The opening Alvin, Erica and Karina stories have no named fund, filing, interview or source in the stored captions. They function as narrative illustrations and cannot be treated as observed cases."", ""UNVERIFIED: The aggregate claims of $15 billion requested, 53% returned across the 12 largest funds, average requests of 12%, 8% of interest income as PIK, 2.8% nonaccruals, and the exact Fitch over-9% comparison lack named tables and measurement definitions in the transcript. They may be plausible but are not independently certified here."", ""MISLEADING: 'outside anybody's ability to tell you what they are worth' overstates valuation uncertainty. Private loans lack continuous exchange prices and estimates can be stale or model-dependent, but managers, auditors and third-party valuation processes do estimate fair value under accounting rules."", ""PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED: The 5% tender structure and public-market discounts demonstrate a liquidity/valuation distinction. A public BDC's discount to NAV is not automatically proof that every underlying loan is overvalued; discounts can also reflect fees, leverage, expected losses, governance, taxes, sentiment and liquidity."", ""UNVERIFIED: The five-year $100,000 comparisons ($181,000 total U.S. stock market, $156,000 private credit, $122,000 high yield) omit exact tickers/indexes, start/end dates, reinvestment, fees and tax assumptions, so they are not reproducible from the stored text."", ""SUPPORTED_WITH_QUALIFICATION: DOL's proposal explicitly requires fiduciaries to consider performance, fees, liquidity, valuation, benchmarks and complexity. This supports the video's relevance to retirement savers while cutting against the implication that alternatives can be inserted without fiduciary review.""], ""ending_words"": ""So, the next time somebody shows you an investment with a line that never goes down, do not ask what it earned, ask what s