 ""UNKNOWN"", ""image_path"": ""research/finance-economics-intelligence/audit-batches/NICK_RgaTGzeFcPQ.jpg"", ""image_sha256"": ""751b4a780d8560eb78149759178bf16d2ca33a8ce2db317893731cc54beef1cf"", ""image_source"": ""https://i.ytimg.com/vi/RgaTGzeFcPQ/maxresdefault.jpg"", ""mobile_review_width"": 320, ""performance_effect"": ""NOT_ESTABLISHED"", ""review_scope"": ""ACTUAL_IMAGE"", ""source_refs"": [""VIDEO_MASTER.csv:RgaTGzeFcPQ"", ""THUMBNAIL_COVERAGE.csv:RgaTGzeFcPQ"", ""audit-batches/NICK_156_READ_RECEIPTS.json""]}","{""analysis"": ""The script is a balanced narrative essay rather than a valuation model. It concedes network resilience and scarcity evidence, then distinguishes literal protocol failure from investor loss and time-horizon risk. Recurring Lindsay, Dale and Hollis stories make abstract mechanisms concrete, but they are illustrative composites, not documented cases. Several dated market figures are directionally supported, yet the script repeatedly converts vendor estimates or draft proposals into precise facts without naming the dataset, calculation date or uncertainty. It never estimates a defensible probability of zero and should not: Bitcoin has no cash-flow valuation anchor, market paths are uncertain, and survival does not guarantee a positive return. The close appropriately permits no position, but the thumbnail overstates the conclusion."", ""audio_verified"": false, ""availability"": ""TEXT_AVAILABLE"", ""beat_map"": [""Contrarian zero-question hook and fictional Lindsay/Dale/Hollis characters"", ""Price drawdown versus prior Bitcoin bear markets"", ""Network-attack pathway dismissed using hash-rate and attack-cost claims"", ""ETF flows, miner sales and treasury-company liquidity as structural selling"", ""Bull case from failed obituaries, long-held supply, lost coins and issuance"", ""Holder losses, ownership estimates and typical position-size framing"", ""Reframe from literal zero to long-lived capital impairment"", ""Halving and fee-based security-budget problem"", ""Draft quantum-resistant address and migration proposals"", ""Three-question decision framework and non-position conclusion""], ""claim_audit"": [""SUPPORTED WITH DATE LIMIT: SEC filings describe Bitcoin above $126,000 in 2025 and Strategy reported $64,164 on 2026-07-24. Using $126,000 and $65,000 gives a 48.41% drawdown. Those endpoints do not prove one continuous October-to-recording series without the named price source and timestamp."", ""ARITHMETIC SUPPORTED: $67,600 to $15,700 is a 76.78% decline. The broader claim that every prior bear market lost 77%-93% depends on cycle definitions and an unnamed Fidelity analysis, so it is not independently established here."", ""UNVERIFIED PRECISION: Record hash rate may show continuing computation but does not prove economic security under every attack. The $10 billion hardware and $1.5 million-per-hour attack estimates omit hardware availability, topology, electricity prices, attack duration, defensive response and the distinction between hash control and guaranteed successful double spending."", ""PARTLY SUPPORTED: IBIT's SEC filing says U.S. spot Bitcoin products had their largest quarterly net outflows since launch in Q2 2026. It does not establish the script's exact June $4.0-$4.5 billion aggregate, BlackRock 79% share or claim that ETF flows explain 45% of weekly price movement; the script names no reproducible study or provider series."", ""PARTLY SUPPORTED, AGGREGATE UNVERIFIED: MARA disclosed about $1.5 billion of Q1 2026 Bitcoin sales to reduce debt, showing miner liquidity-driven selling. That filing does not prove the industry-wide 32,000-BTC total, comparison with all 2025, hashprice in the high $20s, or a universal $35 break-even. Those require a defined miner set and unit methodology."", ""MISSTATED AT PUBLICATION: Strategy's June 29 program allowed up to $1.25 billion of Bitcoin sales for its USD reserve, and its July 5 filing said the entire capacity remained available. Authorization was not a completed 20,000-coin sale. A later 10-Q reports actual July sales and roughly 843,775 coins at July 24, but that filing postdates the July 23 video and cannot validate publication-time sourcing."", ""DIRECTIONALLY SUPPORTED, CAUSAL OVERREACH: ETF redemptions, miner costs and treasury-company dividends can create selling independent of belief. Calling funds, miners and treasury companies the three largest structural holders and saying all became net sellers in the same six months requires consistent stock/flow definitions; Strategy remained a large net buyer during the first half of 2026."", ""UNVERIFIED VENDOR DATA: The 475-obituary count, 22 Peter Schiff entries, 14.8 million long-term-holder coins, 566 coins aging daily, 2.3-5 million permanently lost, 10.83 million underwater coins and 95% short-term-holder loss rate are not tied to primary records in the transcript. Wallet dormancy does not prove one owner, permanent loss or intent to hold."", ""ARITHMETIC CONDITIONAL: Investing $100 on each of 471 alleged obituary dates means $47,100 contributed. The asserted 1,043 BTC and roughly $67 million require the exact date-price convention, fees and a current price; the batch cannot reproduce them from the transcript alone. Calling it the most effective strategy ever is hyperbole, not an exhaustive investment comparison."", ""SUPPORTED SURVEY VALUE, WRONG LABEL: The Federal Reserve's probability-based survey of nearly 13,000 adults reports 10% used cryptocurrency for investment or transactions in 2025. It does not measure all-time ownership, and 10% cannot be directly compared with differently worded volunteer surveys as if each estimates the same population quantity."", ""ARITHMETIC SUPPORTED: A 43% loss requires a 75.44% gain to break even. At the stated $112,500 purchase midpoint and $65,000 current price, the loss is 42.22% and the required recovery is 73.08%; rounded narrative inputs explain the difference."", ""SUPPORTED PROTOCOL SCHEDULE, ECONOMICS UNCERTAIN: Bitcoin's subsidy halves every 210,000 blocks. Three halvings reduce 3.125 BTC to 0.390625 BTC, one eighth, around 2036 subject to block timing. If fees are only 0.61% of current miner revenue and total real revenue must stay constant, fees would need to grow about 143.6x after that subsidy decline. Neither the 0.61% input nor constant required security spending is established, and price, difficulty, energy cost, hardware efficiency and miner composition can change."", ""MISCHARACTERIZED TECHNICAL STATUS: BIP-360 is a draft proposal in the BIP repository, not merged activation in Bitcoin Core. BIP-361 is also draft and describes phased restrictions plus proposed rescue protocols; it is not an adopted decision to confiscate or permanently freeze a third of supply. Its own 34% exposed-public-key estimate is a proposal input, not proof those coins will be lost."", ""SPECULATION, NOT FACT: 'Almost certainly not' and any five-to-forty-year quantum timeline are judgments. No defensible probability of Bitcoin reaching zero, recovering within a holding period, or facing cryptographically relevant quantum attack can be calculated from the cited public material."", ""INVESTMENT-RISK LIMIT: Bitcoin can experience extreme volatility, liquidity shocks, custody loss, regulatory change, protocol/governance conflict, leverage cascades, dilution through wrappers or treasury vehicles and permanent capital loss without literally trading at zero. The audit is evidence review, not investment advice.""], ""ending_words"": ""That is the whole test. Everything else is just somebody's story about why the next buyer is going to show up."", ""opening_words"": ""Nobody who says Bitcoin is going to zero actually believes Bitcoin is going to zero."", ""review_scope"": ""FULL_STORED_TEXT"", ""source"": {""Caption_type"": ""auto_generated"", ""Dataset"": ""DS-000022"", ""Duplicate_of"": """", ""Evidence_locator"": ""data/extracted/channel-data/DS-000022/packages/nick-invests/Nick